comments.body:
Finally got around to testing this.  I love the features!

This is so much more than just a layer manager, it is an element manager. the ability to name elements, and to select them in the manager not in the scene holds lots of potential. I am now thinking this should be combined with other features/scripts such as presenter notes for slides. That however would require first a definition of the shared customData type.

As a UX it would be great to display thumbnails of selected elements such as a thumbnail for a group of elements.

Unfortunately, however, I haven't yet gotten deep with testing, but already ran into some issues. I created layers, then switched to markdown view mode (to observe the data in the Excalidraw json). When I switched back to Excalidraw view mode the layers were not loaded - layer manager was uninitialized. I had to stop and start layer manager for the layers to load again. Later I noticed that switching leaves to another tab and back to the drawing reloads layer manager.

I like how data is handled under custom data, however, I don't understand the new "name" property. Why is this needed on top of the customData.lmx?

```json
"customData": {
  "lmx": {
	  "label": "My element",
	  "groupLabels": {
		  "Group": "Group"
	  }
  }
},
"name": "My element",
```

Even after I close layer manager, it automatically restarts when I navigate to an Excalidraw drawing. It's as if there was an event handler that wasn't clean up when closing layer manager. I see a risk of memory leak. I am now unsure how many instances of layer managers are running in memory, and if the instance lifecycle is handled robust enough.
